  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Isolated showers and thunderstorms are forecast to \ndevelop along the sea breeze this afternoon.\n\nEarly this morning, satellite water vapor shows dry air building \neast of the Southern Appalachians with the passage of H5 trough. The \ntrough axis is timed to push over the CWA by 15Z, sliding offshore \nbetween 18-21Z. PW values across the forecast area will begin the \nday in excess of 2.2\", before falling to below 1.7\" by late \nthis afternoon. Forecast soundings shows deep dry air increasing\nabove H6 this afternoon, with a significant inversion centered \nat H65. High resolution guidance shows isolated showers and \nthunderstorms developing near the sea breeze this afternoon. \nHowever, with increasing dry air, shallow lapse rates, and a H65\ninversion any convection should remain general. High \ntemperatures should rise above yesterday's values, ranging \nbetween 90 to 95 degrees.",
